course: dictionary
lesson: 10826
title: Word in context: velociraptor
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words come with a picture already in your head, and that picture can be wrong. Velociraptor is a good example. Films show it as huge and scaly, but the context in a text can correct the picture. «In the films, raptors are as tall as a man, scaly, and clever enough to open doors, but the real Velociraptor was about the size of a turkey and covered in feathers.»
explain: Look for clue words. The word «but» tells you the sentence is about to contrast two things, the film version and the real one. The real one is smaller and has feathers. Always check the clue by swapping your meaning into the sentence: a turkey-sized, feathered dinosaur fits «the real Velociraptor», so your new picture makes sense.
explain: Other sentences add more clues. «Most raptors were small» tells you that Utahraptor, at about 6 metres long, was an unusual giant and not the usual size. When you read science, use the clues in the text first, and use a dictionary or a teacher to check what you are not sure of.
fact: A velociraptor was a small, fast, meat-eating dinosaur.
fact: Velociraptors lived in what is now Mongolia and China.
fact: A velociraptor ran on two legs, had feathers, and had a large curved claw on each foot.
fact: Films such as «Jurassic Park» show velociraptors as much bigger and scalier than real fossils show.
fact: Context clues help: «but», «most» and «the real» all tell you that the text is correcting a wrong picture.
exercise: «In the films, raptors are as tall as a man, but the real Velociraptor was about the size of a turkey.» How big was a real velociraptor? | As tall as a man | As heavy as a polar bear | *About the size of a turkey | As big as a house
exercise: What did a velociraptor have on each foot? | Round pads like a dog | Hooves like a horse | Webbed toes like a duck | *A large curved claw
exercise: «Birds evolved from small feathered meat-eating dinosaurs called theropods, the group of T. rex and Velociraptor.» Which group does velociraptor belong to? | Mammals | Insects | Fish | *Theropods
test: «A famous fossil shows a velociraptor fighting a protoceratops.» Where did the velociraptor live? | Antarctica | *Mongolia and China | Scotland | Australia
test: How did a velociraptor move about? | On four legs like a horse | By swimming in lakes | *On two legs | By flying through the air
exam: Which description of a velociraptor is best? | A fish that lived in the sea | A slow plant-eating dinosaur with a long neck | *A small, fast, meat-eating dinosaur with feathers and a large curved claw on each foot | A huge, scaly dinosaur as tall as a man
